// An account hook (CESVM trigger). A GATE runs BEFORE an incoming transfer
// commits and decides accept (clean return) or reject (require fails / abort).
// A reject fails the transfer as a courtesy signal to the sender.
//
// The event descriptor is in the `input` region:
//   input[0..3] = counterparty pubkey (the sender)
//   input[4]    = amount
//   input[5]    = this account's balance at fire time
// and `invoke_kind` says which event fired (INVOKE_XFER_IN for an inbound
// wire transfer). See docs/cesl.md, section "Account hooks".
//
// This gate accepts inbound transfers of at least 1 whole credit and rejects
// everything smaller - a minimum-deposit policy. It only screens inbound
// transfers; any other invocation just accepts.
//
// Deploy: compile, create an IMMUTABLE asset with the bytecode, then point
// your account's alias at it as a GATE (op = ALIAS_OP_HOOK_GATE, content =
// the asset key). Gates run on the free grant only (no refill), so keep them
// cheap. Amounts below the dust floor never fire a hook at all.

if (invoke_kind == INVOKE_XFER_IN) {
  require(input[4] >= PRICE_UNIT);   // at least 1.0 credit, else reject
}
return 0;
